{title: Faith Without Works}
{subtitle: James 2:17}
{key: D}
{tempo: 156}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]What good is it, my brothers
If someone says he has faith
[G]But does not have works
Can [A]that faith save him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]If a brother or sister is poorly clothed
And lacking daily food
And you say, [G]go in peace, be warm and filled
Without [A]giving what they need
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Faith without [A]works is [G]dead
[D]Faith without [A]works is [G]dead
[D]Show me your [A]faith with [G]nothing to show
I'll [D]show you my [A]faith by what I [G]do
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]So also faith by itself
If it does not have works
Is [G]dead, is dead
Get [A]up and give
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [G] | [D] | [A] | [G] | ×2
| [G] |
